# NAQUUUU hub line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: `core.autocrlf=true` is set on this Windows host and there
# was no .gitattributes, so nothing structurally prevented a Windows checkout from
# rewriting the POSIX shell hooks in .githooks/ with CRLF line endings.
#
# That matters more than usual here, because these two files ARE the sanitization
# gate and the force-push block. A CRLF-mangled `#!/bin/sh` shebang is not a syntax
# error - Git simply stops executing the hook. Both gates then fail OPEN with no
# error, no output, and no commit block. A silent gate is worse than a broken one,
# because it reports success.
#
# Fix: pin LF on anything executed by a POSIX shell. Leave everything else alone so
# this file does not force a repo-wide line-ending surprise on Windows.

# The gate hooks themselves. Highest priority: their shebang must stay LF.
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-push    text eol=lf

# Shell scripts, both the repo copies and any installed to ~/.local/bin.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# GitHub-provided merge driver helper, if ever added.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
